  "preamble": "Substitution of the voiced pharyngeal fricative [ʕ] by the voiced uvular fricative [ʁ] in Arabic loanwords in Kipchak Turkic languages, which lack pharyngeals. Kazakh and Bashkir render Arabic ʿayn as ғ [ʁ] (Bashkir also [ɢ]) before back vowels, as in Kazakh ғылым 'science' from ʿilm.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Retraction, Loanword Adaptation",
  "languageExamples": [
    {
      "language": "Kazakh",
      "languageFamily": "Kipchak",
      "examples": [
        {
          "from": "Arabic عِلْم ʿilm 'knowledge' [ʕ]",
          "to": "ғылым [ʁəˈləm] 'science'"
        },
        {
          "from": "Arabic عَرْش ʿarš 'throne' [ʕ]",
          "to": "ғарыш [ʁɑˈrəʃ] 'outer space'"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "Bashkir",
      "languageFamily": "Kipchak",
      "examples": [
